infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Omit vs DistributiveOmit on a discriminated union
  desc keyof a union is only its shared keys — distribution runs Omit per variant
  compares
    - label Omit<T, K> (stdlib, non-distributive)
      children
        - label Def: Pick<T, Exclude<keyof T, K>>
          desc Operates on T as one whole type
        - label keyof (Circle | Square) = "kind"
          desc A union's keys are only those shared by every member
        - label Omit<Shape, "kind"> -> {}
          desc Remove the one shared key and nothing is left
        - label Variant keys never appear
          desc radius and side were never in keyof Shape
    - label DistributiveOmit<T, K> (opt-in)
      children
        - label Def: T extends unknown ? Omit<T, K> : never
          desc Naked-parameter conditional forces distribution
        - label Omit runs once per member
          desc Circle and Square are handled separately
        - label -> { radius: number } | { side: number }
          desc Each variant keeps its own keys minus K
        - label The per-variant result you expected
          desc The one-line fix for the union trap
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
